# Clean Code Rules for mk-art-fare Frontend

## Component Structure

### Use Addons Pattern for Complex Components

All complex components with subcomponents MUST follow the Addons pattern:

```
ComponentName/
├── Addons/
│   ├── components/      # All subcomponents
│   └── types/          # Shared types
├── index.tsx           # Main component (default export)
└── styles.ts           # Component styles
```

### Nested Components

When a component has its own subcomponents, nest using the same Addons pattern:

```
ParentComponent/
├── Addons/
│   └── components/
│       └── ChildComponent/
│           ├── Addons/
│           │   └── components/
│           │       └── GrandchildComponent/
│           ├── index.tsx
│           └── styles.ts
```

### File Naming and Exports

- ✅ Component files: `index.tsx` with **default export**
- ✅ Style files: `styles.ts` in same directory as component
- ✅ Type files: `Addons/types/index.ts`
- ❌ No named exports for components
- ❌ No styles in parent when child needs them

## TypeScript Standards

### No Type Casting

❌ **Never**:
```typescript
const value = data as SomeType;
const value: any = data;
```

✅ **Always**:
```typescript
// Use discriminated unions
type FieldValue = TextFieldValue | NumberFieldValue | SelectFieldValue;

// Let TypeScript narrow types
switch (field.type) {
  case FieldType.TEXT:
    // TypeScript knows this is TextFieldValue
    return field.value.toUpperCase();
}
```

### No Defensive Type Checking

❌ **Never**:
```typescript
const value = typeof data === 'string' ? data : JSON.stringify(data);
```

✅ **Always**:
```typescript
// Define proper types, trust them
const value = data; // Database handles JSON automatically
```

## React Patterns

### Use useMemo for Conditional Rendering

❌ **Never**:
```typescript
{fieldType && (() => {
  switch (fieldType) {
    case 'text': return <Input />;
    case 'number': return <InputNumber />;
  }
})()}
```

✅ **Always**:
```typescript
const inputField = useMemo(() => {
  switch (fieldType) {
    case 'text': return <Input />;
    case 'number': return <InputNumber />;
  }
}, [fieldType]);

return <>{inputField}</>;
```

## Styling

### Minimize Ant Design Customization

❌ **Avoid**:
```typescript
const CustomButton = styled(Button)`
  background: blue;
  border-radius: 8px;
`;
```

✅ **Prefer**:
```typescript
<Button type="primary" shape="round">
```

### Component-Specific Styles

- Each component should have its own `styles.ts` if it needs custom styling
- Don't mix styles from different components in a shared file
- Keep styles co-located with components

## Database

### JSON Columns

- Use native JSON columns in database
- No manual `JSON.stringify()` or `JSON.parse()` in services
- Trust MySQL to handle JSON serialization

## File Organization

```
src/
├── components/           # Shared/reusable components
├── pages/
│   └── dashboard/
│       └── PageName/
│           ├── Addons/
│           │   ├── components/
│           │   └── types/
│           ├── index.tsx
│           └── styles.ts
├── services/            # API/RTK Query
└── types/              # Global types
```

## Import Order

```typescript
// 1. React and third-party
import { FC, useMemo } from 'react';
import { Form, Input } from 'antd';

// 2. Global types and services
import { FieldType } from '@/types/fields';
import { useGetDataQuery } from '@/services/apiSlice';

// 3. Local imports (styles, types, components)
import { ComponentStyled } from './styles';
import { LocalType } from './Addons/types';
import SubComponent from './Addons/components/SubComponent';
```

